  "question": {
    "text": "Out of 11 consecutive natural number if three numbers are selected at random (without repetition), then the probability that they are in A.P. with positive common difference is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>101</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>101</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>33</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>99</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>sum of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>&#38;</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;is even and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;depends on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>&#38;</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p>Thus, we can not choose all three independently, but we can&nbsp;choose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>&#38;</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p>Moreover,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math> should be&nbsp;both&nbsp;either even or odd as their sum is even.</p><p>Out of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>&nbsp;consecutive natural numbers, either&nbsp;five&nbsp;are&nbsp;even and six are&nbsp;odd or&nbsp;six are&nbsp;even and five are odd.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>6</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>11</mn></mmultiscripts></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>6</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>11</mn></mmultiscripts></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>33</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
